<Base title="Inside Medscan | The records behind the report" description="How Medscan connects health and billing APIs, creates signed QR reports, and keeps private questions behind patient permissions."><section class="wrap about-hero"><a class="text-link" href="/">← Back to Medscan</a><p class="intro">The engineering behind the connection</p><h1 class="hero-title">Separate records.<br/>Shared context.</h1><p class="lede">Medscan explores a practical question: can fragmented health and billing records become a useful, inspectable conversation?</p></section><section class="wrap about-body"><h2>Each system owns its facts.</h2><div><p>Health, billing, access, knowledge and reports each own their data. The context layer joins them through HTTP APIs, rather than reaching into another module’s database tables.</p><p>Postgres holds the authoritative records. A separate, replaceable Neo4j projection supports relationship questions. Everyday counts, balances and lab results use the Health and Billing APIs.</p></div><h2>A report is a snapshot.</h2><div><p>Reports store their context and render it as HTML or a PDF. A signed QR code connects that report to the app. The QR payload carries no patient data.</p><p>The saved summary and current records serve different purposes. Medscan keeps that distinction visible instead of silently substituting one for the other.</p></div><h2>Permission is part of every answer.</h2><div><p>General knowledge is public. Private questions verify identity, map it to an internal user and check explicit PatientAccess permissions. Sign-in alone does not grant access to a patient.</p><p>The hosted preview uses Cognito sign-in. Automatic demo identity is a local development feature and is disabled in Lambda.</p></div><h2>A proof of concept, with honest limits.</h2><div><p>This is not a production healthcare system, a diagnostic tool or an unrestricted medical chatbot. It uses synthetic data and deterministic supported questions, with reviewed educational sources.</p><p>Live hospital integrations, clinical predictions and a general AI assistant remain future work. Physical device and hosted sign-in acceptance are separate verification steps.</p><a class="button" href={site.app}>Open hosted demo <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><a class="text-link" href={site.source}>View on Atriveo ↗</a></div></section></Base>
